# #1736 row 1 with main suspended INSIDE a try: the stop is not an error
# delivered to main, so the catch never runs. g_try_depth is process-global,
# and main's open try suppresses the dying task's own trace print, so the stop
# prints the error itself — a fail-fast stop is never silent.
# Expected: the error text, rc 1, and none of AFTER_YIELD / CAUGHT / MARK_END.
define die() as:
    missing
d is task_spawn of die
task_detach of d
try:
    task_yield of null
    print of "AFTER_YIELD"
catch e:
    print of f"CAUGHT {e.kind}"
print of "MARK_END"
